worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dd27bde0e4244fdaa6cbf12d593d53d628b335d439e5ac5f092446d750ee8dfd" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/state.json" "file_sha256" "6851404c2d0c65d959e2449c4003fc6a09dddc6f00bdabca3d031182dbe407f3" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/example-4697.json" "file_sha256" "e0d5a1f73737319b54db36b2547533ed708af22c366448ceda6e5b0cdfb1c811" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y=0 \\\\ y=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/example-4697.json" "file_sha256" "e0d5a1f73737319b54db36b2547533ed708af22c366448ceda6e5b0cdfb1c811" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=5 \\\\ x-6y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/example-4698.json" "file_sha256" "afc139329376e0a05d6ed72282b22003fff2a5214a1d13566f15ba6b0c3f7125" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-5 \\\\ y=-10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/example-4698.json" "file_sha256" "afc139329376e0a05d6ed72282b22003fff2a5214a1d13566f15ba6b0c3f7125" "basis" 1421 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040213/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-130909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-130909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & y=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{9}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-20461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{4}{2}$ and $y=\\frac{15}{2}$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{9}{2}$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=3$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-\\frac{17}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\  & y=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-1059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -16\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=17$ and $y=-16$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=10$ and $y=11$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=13$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=13$ and $y=14$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+7y=-2 \\\\  & y=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7(-1)=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2+7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5$ and $y=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-130910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=-2$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=15$ and $y=1$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=2$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=13$ and $y=-1$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-130910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-1060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{11}{16}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{15}{16}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{16}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{16}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-1060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-73544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-4y=6 \\\\  & 4x-7y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-73544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=3 \\\\  & y=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-2)=3\\,⇒\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-1$ and $y=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-73544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-73544" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-73544" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=-1$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-2$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-5$ and $y=-4$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=7$ and $y=2$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-73544" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+8y=22 \\\\  & 7x-5y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{71}{3} & -\\frac{142}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{3}{71}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20497" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-20497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20497" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned