estion" "q-20496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+7y=-5 \\\\  & 7x+11y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20496" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & 3x+\\frac{1}{5}y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{4}{5} & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & y=30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=30$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{1}{3}(30)=11\\,⇒\\,x=11-10=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$ and $y=30.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3532eb48af017a328dc0fd3cb6e4d0673fefd98e4b59c2d122fc040f74b7ec1d"} {"question" "q-20500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=12$ and $y=-3$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=0$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=30$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=10$ and $y=3$"] ["text" "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=9$ and $y=6$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "q-20500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=30$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/state.json" "file_sha256" "89e0c09f459534e46c1109024c15894148dae0a560a67a5a106b636428cb401c"} {"question" "e-4697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/67d01790cfbda1f20a23c9e22a64714156485851ce56b2f73e9873db6ef4bed8.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/example-4697.json" "file_sha256" "a4487bff6780e1dcc6099fbec85eff31e7bb8e0d2ed3c303223009a71a25de3d"} {"question" "e-4697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/da9c44be043ad3a15808a9e0dd77636697170047e61b73a0d591bc3581d992fb.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/example-4697.json" "file_sha256" "a4487bff6780e1dcc6099fbec85eff31e7bb8e0d2ed3c303223009a71a25de3d"} {"question" "e-4698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/a80ecf94bbd4f0ea4b7a860e340039ca80bc5ccd0d2a19503cb9dcc571558976.png)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/example-4698.json" "file_sha256" "83d7b7f1b2f9c984e2393dfd4b07d753c70fd6139349858797bb88a62b2a0317"} {"question" "e-4698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/ab29f353f00454b6e8eeb490336e2b33d0b2cf6cd47f4d24ac6c8a8f042af628.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/ee5b759f55931cf4935a0763f22c9eb5deedb04f3e247c295aa2a1da09b121b4.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/example-4698.json" "file_sha256" "83d7b7f1b2f9c984e2393dfd4b07d753c70fd6139349858797bb88a62b2a0317"}] "usage" {"e-4697" [] "e-4698" [] "q-1059" [] "q-130909" [] "q-20496" [] "q-73538" []} "basis" 2598 "retractions" [[17592186059508 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186059508 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y=0 \\\\ y=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$"] [17592186059509 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=5 \\\\ x-6y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [17592186059509 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-5 \\\\ y=-10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186306371 17592186306372 17592186306373 17592186306374 17592186306375 17592186306378 17592186306379 17592186306380 17592186306381 17592186306382 17592186306398 17592186306399 17592186306400 17592186306401 17592186306402 17592186306405 17592186306406 17592186306407 17592186306408 17592186306409] "immutable_fields" [[17592186306370 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306370 :answer-field/id] [17592186306370 :answer-field/key] [17592186306370 :answer-field/type] [17592186306377 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306377 :answer-field/id] [17592186306377 :answer-field/key] [17592186306377 :answer-field/type] [17592186306397 :answer-field/correct] [17592186306397 :answer-field/id] [17592186306397 :answer-field/key] [1